      "name": "Detachment",
      "ownership": {
        "default": 0
      },
      "sort": 50000,
      "system": {
        "_migration": {
          "previous": {
            "foundry": "13.350",
            "schema": 0.948,
            "system": "7.7.3"
          },
          "version": 0.953
        },
        "actionType": {
          "value": "free"
        },
        "actions": {
          "value": null
        },
        "category": "defensive",
        "deathNote": false,
        "description": {
          "gm": "",
          "value": "<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Alekin takes damage that would bring him to or below one of his HP thresholds (320, 240, or 160 HP) for the first time.</p><hr /><p>Instead of taking the full blow, Alekin splits off an Aspect of himself to take the blow for him. Execute the following steps in this order:</p><ol><li><p>Prevent any damage of the triggering damage instance beyond the triggering threshold.</p></li><li><p>Alekin Steps into an unoccupied adjacent space. If there are no eligible spaces, he may teleport to the closest unoccupied space instead.</p></li><li><p>Summon an Aspect into Alekin's old square. The Aspect enters initiative immediately after the current actor's turn.</p></li><li><p>The newly summoned Aspect takes over all effects on Alekin. For the purpose of targeted abilities and immunities like Hunt Prey or Demoralize, the Aspect counts as the old creature, and Alekin counts as a new creature.</p></li></ol><p>Detachment can only trigger once for each threshold.</p><p><strong>Special:</strong> Alekin can use this ability even if an effect would otherwise prevent him from acting.</p>"
        },
        "publication": {
