        "actionType": {
          "value": "passive"
        },
        "actions": {
          "value": null
        },
        "category": "defensive",
        "deathNote": false,
        "description": {
          "gm": "",
          "value": "<p>Alekin's body is just an expendable shell he can summon or destroy at will. He can summon additional bodies to move between, which are called Decoys.</p><p>Whenever at least one Decoy is present, Alekin's soul rapidly moves back and forth between his current body and all Decoys. He is considered to be in all squares occupied by any of his Decoys for the purpose of targeting and effect ranges, and has All-Around Vision as long as at least one Decoy is present.</p><p>If Alekin is targeted by a hostile effect, roll 1d&lt;number of active Decoys + 1&gt;. On a 1, Alekin was inhabiting the targeted Decoy at that moment and takes all effects normally. On any other result, the target was merely a Decoy. If the triggering effect was a successful attack roll that would have dealt damage, or a failed save against a damaging effect, the Decoy is destroyed.</p><p>Some of Alekin's abilities allow him to use Decoys for other purposes. In most cases, any Decoys used for these abilities are then destroyed.</p><p>For the purpose of abilities, the number of active Decoys is always equal to the number of boss tokens on the map, minus 1.</p>"
        },
        "publication": {
          "authors": "",
